    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Iron deficiency anemia in pregnancy (O99.019)</content>. Hemoglobin 10.9 g/dL and ferritin 96 ng/mL four weeks after the first dose: responding. [S]<list><item>Second ferric carboxymaltose 750 mg dose today.</item><item>Blood count and ferritin at 27 weeks.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Fourteenth pregnancy at 37 (O09.529)</content>. Normal anatomy; growth on the 50th centile. The placenta is fundal and clear of the cervix, and she has had no cesarean or other uterine surgery, so there is no placenta previa and the risk of placenta accreta spectrum is low; no repeat placental scan or MRI is needed. Blood pressure 104/62 mmHg. [S]<list><item>Continue aspirin and folic acid.</item><item>Glucose challenge, blood count, and Tdap at 27 weeks.</item><item>Visits every two weeks from 28 weeks.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Blood pressure and urine protein</td><td>Every prenatal visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>104/62 mmHg; urine protein negative</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fetal heart and fundal height</td><td>Every prenatal visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Fetal heart 148 per minute; fundal height 21 cm</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Weight gain</td><td>Every prenatal visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>61.9 kg, up 3.3 kg since intake</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Hemoglobin and ferritin</td><td>At intake, four weeks after starting treatment, at 24 to 28 weeks, and before delivery</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Hemoglobin 10.9 g/dL and ferritin 96 ng/mL after the first intravenous dose; second dose today</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Intravenous iron infusion safety</td><td>With each infusion</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No reaction to the first dose; second dose given with 30 minutes of observation, no reaction</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Detailed anatomy scan with placental location</td><td>At 18 to 22 weeks</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Normal anatomy; estimated weight 410 g; placenta posterior fundal, clear of the os; no signs of accreta</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Repeat placental scan at 32 weeks</td><td>Only if the placenta is low-lying or covers the os</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Placenta well clear of the os</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Low-dose aspirin</td><td>Daily from 12 to 16 weeks until delivery; review at every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Taken nightly; no bruising or bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Gestational diabetes screen</td><td>At 24 to 28 weeks</td><td>Due</td><td>Glucose challenge booked for 27 weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Perinatal mood screen (EPDS)</td><td>Each trimester</td><td>Due</td><td>Second-trimester screen at 27 weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Postpartum hemorrhage risk assessment and birth plan</td><td>At intake, in the third trimester, and on admission for birth</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No placenta previa or accreta; risk factors remain grand multiparity and anemia, now improving</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Hemoglobin at least 11 g/dL with replete iron stores before delivery. In progress; target 1631-06-02 [S]</item><item>An informed choice about aneuploidy screening by 14 weeks. Outcome by 1631-02-03: Chose cell-free DNA (low risk) with the nuchal translucency scan (1.7 mm); declined diagnostic testing [S]</item><item>Blood pressure below 140/90 mmHg with aspirin taken nightly from 13 weeks. In progress; target 1631-07-12 [S]</item><item>A written delivery and postpartum hemorrhage plan agreed by 36 weeks, with birth planned in a hospital with a blood bank and operating theatre. In progress; target 1631-06-02 [S]</item><item>A postpartum contraception choice and a plan for the interval before any future pregnancy, made on her own terms before delivery. In progress; target 1631-06-02 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Pregnancy at Age 35 Years or Older: ACOG Obstetric Care Consensus No. 11 (2022); Anemia in Pregnancy: ACOG Practice Bulletin, Number 233 (2021); Aspirin Use to Prevent Preeclampsia and Related Morbidity and Mortality: Preventive Medication (2021); Obstetric Care Consensus No. 7: Placenta Accreta Spectrum (2018)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Prenatal visit at 27 weeks with the glucose challenge, blood count, and Tdap. Next scheduled visit 1631-04-14: prenatal visit at 27 weeks: glucose challenge, blood count, and Tdap. [S]</paragraph></text>

